e</article-title><source>Mil Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>11</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>886</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16435765</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Yeager</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><article-title>Armies of east and southern Africa fighting a guerrilla war with AIDS. Special report: AIDS and the military</article-title><source>AIDS Anal Afr</source><year>1995</year><volume>11</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>10</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12319957</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ross</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Essien</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekong</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Amos</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogungbade</surname><given-names>GO</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><article-title>The impact of a situationally focused individual human immunodeficiency virus/sexually transmitted disease risk reduction intervention on risk behavior in a 1-year cohort of Nigerian military personnel</article-title><source>Mil Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>11</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>970</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17076449</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Sagala</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>HIV/AIDS prevention strategies in the armed forces in sub-Saharan Africa: A critical review</article-title><source>Armed Forces &#x00026; Society</source><year>2008</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>292</fpage><lpage>314</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/0095327X07302976</pub-id></mixed-citation></re