/surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><article-title>HIV/AIDS, the military and the impact on national and international security</article-title><source>Society in Transition</source><year>2001</year><volume>11</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>120</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B29"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Heinecken</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><article-title>Living in Terror. The looming security threat to Southern Africa</article-title><source>African Security Review</source><year>2001</year><volume>11</volume><issue>4</issue><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.iss.co.za/asr/10No4/Heinecken.html">http://www.iss.co.za/asr/10No4/Heinecken.html</ext-link><comment>Accessed 10/12/07.</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B30"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><name><surname>Garrett</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><article-title>HIV and national security: Where are the links?</article-title><source>A Council on Foreign Relations Report</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cfr.org/publication/8256/hiv_and_national_security.html">http://www.cfr.org/publication/8256/hiv_and_national_security.html</ext-link></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B31"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><article-title>UNAIDS Statement to the UN Security Council</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.un.org/News/dh/latest/piotaids.htm">http://www.un.org/News/dh/latest/piotaids.htm</ext-link><comment>10, January 2000. Accessed 10/8/07</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B32"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Van Beelen</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><article-title>HIV/AIDS and the Military: Fighting the War against HIV/STIs,"</article-title><source>Sexual Health Exchange</source><year>2003</year><volume>11</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>6</fpage><lpage>14</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><re